                                    "text": "================================================================================\nrms_true_follower — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA true-RMS envelope: the signal is squared, the power is averaged with a\nsymmetric window, and the square root gives a waveform-independent level. A\nsecond attack/release stage shapes how quickly the reading may move, so it\nstill has musical ballistics. The split matters: averaging the square with\nattack/release directly biases the result upward on low notes (a 100 Hz sine\nreads about +2.7 dB high with 10/500 ms), while a symmetric RMS window reads\nthe same sine at 0.707 of its peak.\n\nSource: Floru, AES 1998, preprint 4703, §1-2 (true RMS detector); Dutilleux,\nDAFx-98, §5.1-5.4 (squarer + averager amplitude follower; RMS + AR-averager).\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. rms_ms — 5…500 ms, default 50 ms\n   Symmetric RMS measurement window. Longer windows give a steadier reading\n   and more lag; 40-60 ms covers one to three cycles of a low tuba note and is\n   the useful default. Very short windows start to follow the waveform itself.\n\n2. attack_ms — 0.5…200 ms, default 5 ms\n   How fast the output reading may rise after the RMS window has moved. Short\n   values keep the tuba's articulation; this stage does not change the RMS\n   calibration.\n\n3. release_ms — 10…4000 ms, default 500 ms\n   How fast the output reading may fall. Long values hold the body through the\n   gaps between valve notes; short values breathe with them.\n\n4. out_db — -24…+24 dB, default 0 dB\n   Level of the control signal on out1. The RMS of a sine sits about 3 dB below\n   its peak, which is correct and intentional.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1: tuba audio (mono).\n- out1: RMS envelope control signal, 0..1 linear before out_db, at audio rate.\n\nNOTES\n- Square -> symmetric average -> root is the RMS order; do not move the root\n  inside the power loop.\n- The output is a control signal, not a monitor signal.\n- No safety limiter, no metering, no gate.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
