                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-17",
                                    "linecount": 37,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 733.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\npeak_ar_follower — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA full-wave peak follower with separate attack and release times: the plainest\nway to turn the tuba's instantaneous amplitude into a control signal. It reacts\nto every rectified sample, so it is the most articulate and the most \"literal\"\nof the batch — good for transient-shaped modulation (filter blips, envelope\naccents), less good for a smooth loudness reading.\n\nSource: Floru, AES 104th Convention 1998, preprint 4703, §1-2 (peak detector);\nDutilleux, DAFx-98, §5.1-5.2 (full-wave detector + AR-averager).\n\nPARAMETERS (3)\n\n1. attack_ms — 0.1…100 ms, default 5 ms\n   Time for the envelope to reach 63% of a rising step. Short values (0.5-2 ms)\n   keep the valve tongue and the lip transient; long values soften the onset.\n\n2. release_ms — 5…2000 ms, default 250 ms\n   Time for the envelope to fall 63% after the input drops. Short is punchy and\n   lets the follower chatter on a decaying note; long holds the body through\n   gaps between notes.\n\n3. out_db — -24…+24 dB, default 0 dB\n   Level of the control signal on out1. 0 dB keeps the envelope in its natural\n   0..1 range; raise it only when feeding something that expects a hotter signal.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1: tuba audio (mono).\n- out1: envelope control signal, 0..1 linear before out_db, at audio rate.\n\nNOTES\n- The output is a control signal, not a monitor signal. Patch it into a\n  modulation input, or listen to it through a VCA.\n- No safety limiter, no metering, no gate.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
