                                    },
                                    "text": "param out_db 0 @min -24 @max 24",
                                    "varname": "out_db"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-21",
                                    "linecount": 42,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 626.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\nlog_db_follower — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA level follower that smooths in decibels instead of in amplitude: rectify,\ntake 20*log10, run the attack/release one-pole on the dB value, convert back.\nThe release therefore falls at a constant dB/s, which is the \"fader\" or opto\nfeel — a long note fades evenly instead of dropping fast at first and then\ncrawling. The floor control keeps log(0) out of the math and defines silence.\n\nSource: Floru, AES 1998, preprint 4703, §2.2.1-2.2.2 (log-domain RMS detector,\ndB-linear integrator), §4.3 (diode log filter); Dutilleux, DAFx-98, §5.2\n(one-pole averager).\n\nPARAMETERS (4)\n\n1. attack_ms — 0.5…500 ms, default 5 ms\n   Time to cover 63% of a rising dB step. Short values snap to the attack;\n   longer values make the envelope lean in behind the note.\n\n2. release_ms — 10…5000 ms, default 500 ms\n   Time to cover 63% of a falling dB step, i.e. most of the audible fade is\n   spread over this time. Long values (2-5 s) give a slow, sustained body.\n\n3. floor_db — -90…-20 dB, default -60 dB\n   Silence floor and noise gate level. Below this the output is exactly zero;\n   raising it cleans up a noisy stage but also shortens the usable tail.\n\n4. out_db — -24…+24 dB, default 0 dB\n   Level of the control signal on out1.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1: tuba audio (mono).\n- out1: envelope control signal, 0..1 linear before out_db, at audio rate.\n\nNOTES\n- The dB domain is why the release is linear in dB, not in amplitude; that is\n  the whole point of this follower, so do not move the smoothing before the log.\n- The floor is subtracted from the linear output, so a signal at the floor reads\n  0 rather than a small DC offset.\n- No safety limiter, no metering, no gate beyond the floor clamp.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
